# Decision Canvas

Spec: DecisionCanvas
Purpose:
  Standard template for every engineering decision. Ensures all
  required inputs are present before a decision is recorded.

Template:
  QUESTION:
    <exact question being answered>

  CONTEXT:
    @context.CTX<id>
    <project state, constraints, history>

  FACTS:
    - @fact.F<id>: <statement>
    - @fact.F<id>: <statement>

  ASSUMPTIONS:
    - @assumption.A<id>: <statement> (confidence: <level>)

  CONSTRAINTS:
    - @constraint.C<id>: <statement>
    - @constraint.C<id>: <statement>

  OPTIONS:
    A. <option A>
    B. <option B>
    C. <option C> (if applicable)

  TRADE-OFFS:
    - @tradeoff.T<id>: <pros/cons summary>

  DECISION:
    <chosen option>

  REASON:
    <why this option beats others>

  RISK:
    <what could go wrong>

  SECURITY_IMPACT:
    <auth/authz/data-classification/attack-surface consequences;
    "none" only when provably out of scope>

  REVERSIBLE:
    true | false
    score: HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW
    (<why: e.g. additive change vs schema/data split>)

  EVIDENCE:
    - @proof.P<id>
    - @test.X<id>

  FOLLOW-UP:
    - <action>
    - <verification>

Rules:
  [DC-01] Decision canvas MUST be complete before DECISION status = APPROVED.
  [DC-02] Missing FACT or CONSTRAINT blocks approval.
  [DC-03] TRADE-OFF section MUST list at least one pro and one con per option.
  [DC-04] REVERSIBLE flag MUST be set for all decisions.
  [DC-05] REVERSIBILITY score LOW routes to stronger review: security
          review + architecture review before implementation (maps to
          Phase 131 risk engine; LOW = multi-gate, HIGH = normal flow).
  [DC-06] SECURITY_IMPACT MUST be filled for security-relevant DECs
          (SEC.* gate categories); a blank field blocks approval.

